{"seconds": 53.2, "exit": 0, "final": "Good! So **Ng6+** is clearly the best move. The main line with best play is **Ng6+ Kg7 Nxf8+ Kh8 Qg8#**, which is mate in 3.\n\n**Best move:** Ng6+\n\n**Main line:** Ng6+ Kg7 Nxf8+ Kh8 Qg8#\n\n**Motif:** fork (the knight on g6 forks king and rook), discovered attack (moving Ne5 discovers attack on f5), attraction (forcing the king to h8 where mate follows)\n\n**Explanation:**\nYour Ne5 can jump to g6 with check, forking the king and the rook on f8. The king has no good escape: if Kg7, you capture the rook with Nxf8+ and finish with Qg8#. If Kg8, the same plan works. If Black takes with hxg6, you recapture Qxg6 with a dominant position. Always look for knight jumps that give check and attack multiple pieces\u2014they often unlock the whole position.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Ng6+\", \"line\": [\"Ng6+\", \"Kg7\", \"Nxf8+\", \"Kh8\", \"Qg8#\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"discoveredAttack\", \"attraction\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2Nn2/3PpPQ1/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 w - - 4 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2Nn2/3PpPQ1/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 w - - 4 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2Nn2/3PpPQ1/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 w - - 4 21", "move": "Nxf7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2Nn2/3PpPQ1/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 w - - 4 21", "move": "Qg6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2Nn2/3PpPQ1/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 w - - 4 21", "move": "Rg7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2Nn2/3PpPQ1/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 w - - 4 21", "move": "Qh5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p2qpp2/1p2Nn2/3PpPQ1/2N1P1R1/PP5P/2R3K1 w - - 4 21", "move": "Nxf6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r2r1k/1b5p/p